    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0526" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg422"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/816.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Algonquin</hi> established radio communication with <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wheeling</hi> today. Consul at Puerto Plata requested to
                    inform commander of <hi rendition="#italic">Algonquin</hi> in case the telegraph
                    lines across the island are cut, and to ask him to communicate immediately with
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Wheeling.</hi>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
